# Client networks with the same IP.

redes-a-cor-do-perfil = The profile color.
redes-a-porta-do-proxy = The proxy port.
redes-escolha-uma-rede-na-lista-para = Choose a network from the list to see its properties.
redes-nenhuma-rede-use-novo-para-criar = No networks. Use New to create the first one.
redes-o-endereco-do-proxy-quase-sempre = The proxy address, almost always 127.0.0.1.
redes-o-item-do-cofre-com-o = The vault item with the proxy user name and password. None: open proxy.
redes-o-nome-do-perfil-nas-listas = The profile name in the lists and at the end of the tab name (web · Client A).
redes-o-usuario-no-servidor-de-salto = The user on the jump server. Empty: the credential user.
redes-quantos-segundos-esperar-o-proxy-responder = How many seconds to wait for the proxy (or the Nebula network) to respond after it starts.
redes-redes = Networks
redes-testar = Test
redes-os-grupos-e-as-conexoes-que = The groups and connections that use this network will inherit the one from the group above. Open sessions continue.
redes-por-onde-as-conexoes-saem-socks5 = How connections go out. SOCKS5 is what the redes/ recipes bring up (microsocks on port 1081). None: the profile only counts for the jump host.
redes-roda-quando-a-ultima-aba-que = Runs when the last tab that uses the profile closes and when the app closes. Empty: the network stays up.
redes-roda-quando-o-proxy-nao-responde = Runs when the proxy doesn't respond, before connecting (for example docker compose up -d). Empty: the network must already be up.
redes-um-servidor-de-salto-que-vem = A jump server that comes before the connection's. Applies to SSH and built-in SFTP; Telnet and FTP don't use it. Empty: no jump.
redes-uma-rede-por-cliente-cada-perfil = One network per client: each profile says how connections go out (a proxy on 127.0.0.1) and how to bring the VPN up and down. Attach the profile to a group or a connection in the Network row of the properties. With the Nebula, OpenVPN, WireGuard, Tailscale and ZeroTier types, the network runs inside the app, only for its own traffic, from the config.yml, the .ovpn, the .conf or the network login. Test brings the network up if it isn't up yet.
redes-comando-para-descer = Command to bring down
redes-comando-para-subir = Command to bring up
redes-cor = Color
redes-credencial-do-salto = Jump credential
redes-esperar-ate-s = Wait up to (s)
redes-host-do-salto = Jump host
redes-porta-do-salto = Jump port
redes-proxy = Proxy
redes-salto = Jump
redes-subir-e-descer = Bring up and down
redes-usuario-do-salto = Jump user
redes-direta = Direct
redes-herdar = Inherit
redes-herdar-de = Inherit ({ $nome })
redes-nova-rede = New network
redes-responde = The network { $nome } responds: the proxy accepted the connection.
redes-sem-proxy = The network { $nome } has no proxy: only the jump counts, and it is checked when connecting.
redes-testando = Testing the network { $nome }…
redes-apagar-a-rede = Delete the network { $nome }?
redes-prefixo-opcao-fixa = Network { $base }
redes-nao-consegui-rodar = couldn't run the command: { $erro }
redes-subindo = Bringing up the network { $nome }…
redes-pronta = Network { $nome } ready.
redes-nao-subiu-codigo = the network { $nome } didn't come up (code { $c })
redes-nao-subiu = the network { $nome } didn't come up
redes-nao-subiu-motivo = the network { $nome } didn't come up: { $linha }
